      "type": "prose",
      "heading": "At a glance",
      "body": "At a glance\n\nThe official Transport Fever 3 system requirements live on the Steam store page for AppID 3493540, where Urban Games publishes the live minimum and recommended PC hardware block. As of 2026-09-28 the Steam listing confirms a 64-bit Windows convention but has not published concrete numbers for every CPU, GPU, RAM, storage, and DirectX category. Players who want to verify their PC before launch should keep the Steam store page bookmarked and re-check it directly once Urban Games posts the final numbers.\n\nTransport Fever 3 System Requirements by Category\n\nThe Steam store page lists PC specs in six standard categories: operating system, processor, memory, graphics, DirectX, and storage. Until Urban Games publishes concrete numbers for each slot, every line below should be read against the live Steam page rather than as a final spec. The Steam page itself is the single source of truth at research date 2026-09-28.\n\nOperating System\n\nThe Steam page reflects the standard 64-bit Windows requirement that current Urban Games Simulation and Transportation titles share. The exact Windows edition field on the Steam page is the live value; this page mirrors it once Urban Games posts the final figure.\n\nProcessor\n\nThe processor slot on the Steam system requirements block covers both minimum and recommended CPU figures. Concrete numbers for Transport Fever 3 are Not announced as of 2026-09-28; check the official Steam store page for updates.\n\nMemory\n\nThe memory slot lists RAM in gigabytes for the minimum and recommended columns. The Steam page will publish the live values; this page does not inherit RAM figures from Transport Fever 2 or Train Fever because those are sibling titles rather than current-game sources.\n\nGraphics\n\nThe graphics slot lists the minimum and recommended GPU. Concrete numbers for Transport Fever 3 are Not announced as of 2026-09-28; check the official Steam store page for updates.\n\nDirectX\n\nThe DirectX slot lists the DirectX runtime required to launch the game. The Steam page is the live source for the exact DirectX version; this page mirrors the figure once Urban Games posts it.\n\nStorage\n\nThe storage slot lists the disk space the launch build needs plus any additional space the Early Access roadmap may require. Concrete storage figures for Transport Fever 3 are Not announced as of 2026-09-28; check the official Steam store page for updates.\n\nHow to Read the Steam Specs Block\n\nThe Steam store page typically shows two parallel columns: minimum and recommended. Minimum covers the floor hardware that loads the simulation at low settings, while recommended describes a smoother target. For a transport simulator with route-building and a large vehicle roster, the recommended column is usually the more useful buying signal.\n\nWhy 64-bit Matters\n\nUrban Games' recent Simulation and Transportation titles ship as 64-bit Windows applications. A 32-bit operating system cannot run Transport Fever 3, so older PCs and many older laptops are out by default regardless of CPU or RAM tier.\n\nStorage Headroom for Early Access\n\nEarly Access titles continue to receive post-launch patches and content additions. Plan extra headroom on top of the launch-day storage figure so that future updates do not force a drive cleanup.\n\nWhere to Confirm the Live Specs\n\nTreat the Steam store page at https://store.steampowered.com/app/3493540 as the single source of truth for Transport Fever 3 system requirements. The Steam Community Hub discussion threads and Urban Games' official communications will surface the same numbers first, and this page mirrors them once they are posted. The page also flags any category the Steam page has not yet populated so players do not act on rumored values."
